## Toolchain Paths

This project auto-detects installed toolchains. If XC32 or the DFP are installed in non-default locations, use one of these options:

1) Pass paths on the make command line (one-off):

```bash
make COMPILER_LOCATION="C:/Program Files/Microchip/xc32/v5.00/bin" \
	DFP="C:/Program Files/Microchip/MPLABX/v6.25/packs/Microchip/PIC32MZ-EF_DFP/1.4.168"
```

2) Set VS Code settings (global) so tasks pick them up automatically:

- `pic32m-dev.xc32CompilerBinDir` → e.g. `C:/Program Files/Microchip/xc32/v5.00/bin`
- `pic32m-dev.dfpPath` → e.g. `C:/Microchip/packs/Microchip/PIC32MZ-EF_DFP/1.4.168`

3) No MPLAB X installed? Place the DFP standalone here and point DFP to it:

- `C:/Microchip/packs/Microchip/PIC32MZ-EF_DFP/<version>`

Then build as usual:

```bash
make
```

